description: Project memory, documentation upkeep, testing, and secret rules for the job application agent
alwaysApply: true
---

# Project memory

- Read `CURSOR.md` at the start of every task before exploring the codebase. Use it and the linked `docs/` instead of re-reading the whole repo.
- Work phase by phase per `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`. Stop at the end of each phase and wait for user confirmation.

# For every new or changed function, endpoint, task, connector, or page

1. Add or update automated tests (unit, integration, smoke, or frontend). No manual-only verification.
2. Update `CURSOR.md`: the functionality inventory row, the current phase, and a one-line dated change log entry.
3. Update `README.md` when setup, features, commands, or status change.
4. Update the relevant `docs/` file if an architecture decision, API contract, or data model changes.

# Secrets and personal data (public repository)

- Never commit real credentials, tokens, OAuth client secrets, resumes, or personal profile data.
- Committed config uses only `dummy-*` placeholder values (allowlisted in `.gitleaks.toml`).
- Real values belong in `.env`, `secrets/`, or `storage/` (gitignored).
- Run `gitleaks git .` before committing; CI also blocks leaks.

# Safety

- Never enable live application submission or email sending by default.
- All submission paths go through `ApplicationOrchestrator`; never call a channel from a route.
- Do not invent API capabilities or bypass platform restrictions.
